comments.body:
[suggestion] Does it make sense to define an at-rule params regex outside the loop?

E.g.

```js
/** @type {RegExp | undefined} */
let atRuleParamsRegex;
if (!exceptExactValue) {
	if (primary === 'prefix') {
		atRuleParamsRegex = /[<>]/;
	} else if (primary === 'context') {
		atRuleParamsRegex = /(?:min|max)-/i;
	}
}

root.walkAtRules(atRuleRegexes.mediaName, (atRule) => {
	if (atRuleParamsRegex && !atRuleParamsRegex.test(atRule.params)) return;
```

